zuxlsx bundles third-party source code under src/vendor/. Provenance for every
bundled source -- upstream repository, release tag, commit, license and the
local patches applied -- is recorded in tools/vendor/manifest.tsv, with
per-file checksums of the copy as committed in tools/vendor/checksums.sha256.
tools/vendor/verify re-checks all of that offline.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
xlsxio (src/vendor/xlsxio/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  https://github.com/brechtsanders/xlsxio
Release:   0.2.36 (commit a9016eb2eb46dcd613a68fcfcd1002b5adf64ae9)
License:   MIT, reproduced verbatim in src/vendor/xlsxio/LICENSE.txt

  Copyright (c) 2016 Brecht Sanders

Only the XLSX *reader* is bundled: xlsxio_read.c, xlsxio_read_sharedstrings.c
and their headers. The writer (xlsxio_write.c) is deliberately not bundled --
writing workbooks is out of scope (design section 21).

The bundled copy carries two local patches, in tools/patches/xlsxio/, applied
in order. Neither is upstream.

  0001-miniz-zip-backend.patch
      Adds a USE_MINIZ backend beside the existing USE_MINIZIP /
      USE_MINIZIP_NG / libzip ones, so the reader drives miniz's ZIP reader
      (mz_zip_reader_init_file, _locate_file_v2, _extract_iter_new/_read/_free)
      instead of requiring system minizip or libzip. Upstream has no miniz
      backend. Written in the utopp/pkg-xlsx prototype.

  0002-namespace-insensitive-relationship-id.patch
      Looks a worksheet's relationship id up as "id" rather than the literal
      "r:id", so that a workbook binding the OOXML relationships namespace to
      some other prefix still resolves. Written for zuxlsx.

  0003-expose-cell-type-and-number-format.patch
      Reports a cell's OOXML type (t=) rather than only whether it is a shared
      string, and parses xl/styles.xml so that a cell's number format can say
      whether the number it holds is a date. Upstream located the styles part
      and freed the name without opening it. Adds two accessors; changes no
      existing signature. Written for zuxlsx.

  0004-expose-workbook-date-epoch.patch
      Reports workbookPr/@date1904, the epoch a date serial counts from. The
      two systems differ by four years and a day, and xlsxio never read the
      attribute. Written for zuxlsx.

  0005-tolerant-part-name-lookup.patch
      Matches archive members the way OOXML compares part names: backslashes
      folded to forward slashes, ASCII case folded, first match winning so
      that a duplicated part name resolves by position rather than by a lookup
      flag. Upstream matched stored names literally. Written for zuxlsx.

Running the five patches in order against the pristine 0.2.36 release archive
reproduces src/vendor/xlsxio/ byte for byte, including line endings. No other
modification is made to the bundled code, and it is never edited in place:
tools/vendor/fetch re-derives it, and tools/vendor/verify checks the result.

Line endings are CRLF, as shipped by upstream, except on the lines the five
patches introduce. They are deliberately not normalised, so the kept files
still match the release archive.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test fixtures (tests/testthat/sheets/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Seven interoperability workbooks are copied from the readxl project and are
not part of the installed package.

Upstream:  https://github.com/tidyverse/readxl
Commit:    47f8aeac0a99eee6c6db2d64ead2225e5e3ae4af
License:   MIT, reproduced in tests/testthat/sheets/LICENSE-readxl.md

Per-file provenance and checksums are in tests/testthat/sheets/MANIFEST.tsv,
which tools/vendor/verify also checks.
